   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation\nto eligibility requirements for horses participating in the three racing\nlevels of the New York Sire Stakes program",
    "basePrintNo": "S9183",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9183-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §334, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9183\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in\nrelation to eligibility requirements for horses participating in the\nthree racing levels of the New York Sire Stakes program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill clarifies eligibility for participation in the New York Sire\nStakes program by providing that any horse sired by a registered stal-\nlion standing in New York State is eligible to compete, regardless of\nwhere the mare was bred or foaled. Existing language that allows bonus\nawards for those mares residing in New York in the year of conception\nshall be preserved.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends subdivision 1 of section 334 of the Racing,\nPari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law to provide that all horses sired\nby a registered New York stallion are eligible for the three racing\nlevels of the New York Sire Stakes program, including the New York Sires\nStakes, Excelsior Series and County Fairs.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York Sire Stakes program, which includes the Sire Stakes (A\nlevel), Excelsior Series and County Fair races, was established to\npromote the breeding, ownership, and racing of standardbred horses with-\nin New York State. However, current statutory and regulatory language\nhas led to ambiguity and uneven interpretation as to whether horses\nsired by registered New York stallions but conceived outside the state\nare eligible for all of these races in the New York Sire Stakes program.\nThis amendment ensures that eligibility is tied directly to the\nstallion's standing in New York, which is consistent with the program's\nintent to incentivize the state's stallion industry and enhance economic\nactivity surrounding New York's standardbred breeding farms.\n\nBy guaranteeing eligibility for all horses sired by a New York stallion,\nthe bill will encourage greater investment in New York stallions,\nsupport local breeding operations and agricultural employment, eliminate\nconfusion surrounding eligibility standards, and strengthen the competi-\ntiveness of New York's harness racing industry with other state's stan-\ndardbred racing programs.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
